title: NIKKE PC Launcher Dropping K2F Persistence DLL platform_experience_helper.dll
id: 33b2063c-436d-44d9-98db-8d28d828bdca
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects creation of platform_experience_helper.dll, the secondary Windows
    DLL pushed by the tampered NIKKE PC launcher. Attackers modified four
    JavaScript files on Level Infinite's CDN from 27 September 2026 and the
    embedded CEF launcher executed them with its privileges, pulling the LuaJIT
    insight.bundle and a K2F remote-access agent that survived launcher exit.
    The named DLL is the documented on-disk persistence artifact and is the
    point where a post-compromise hunt becomes concrete; correlate with the
    string k2f_chan in the launcher's intl_service debug log.
references:
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/nikke-pc-game-launcher-hacked-to-spread-remote-access-data-stealing-malware/
    - https://gist.github.com/MotherSphere/d6c049a09ba8ac3085c51ee9df24a4e5
    - https://cyberinsider.com/nikke-pc-launcher-malware-remote-access-tool/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/05
tags:
    - attack.t1195
    - attack.t1105
    - attack.t1555
logsource:
    category: file_event
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_filename:
        TargetFilename|endswith: '\platform_experience_helper.dll'
    condition: selection_filename
falsepositives:
    - Any legitimate developer or publisher component that happens to reuse this generic-sounding helper name - verify the signed publisher and the parent launcher before isolating, and sweep the host for insight.bundle and the k2f_chan log string
level: high
